{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree\/reingoldTilfordLayout()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"relatedModules":["Trees"],"name":"GraphDrawing"}],"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"Trees","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reingoldTilfordLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift#L37","fileName":"ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift"},"symbolKind":"method","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}]},"externalID":"s:5Trees10RootedTreeV12GraphDrawingE21reingoldTilfordLayoutAD0E0VyxGyF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"reingoldTilfordLayout()"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tidy drawing of the tree: Reingold and Tilford’s layered tree drawing as Walker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refined it, in Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert’s linear-time form."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees\/rootedtree\/reingoldtilfordlayout()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reingoldTilfordLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The root is at (0, 0) and a vertex at depth d has y = d. Children are placed left to right","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in ","type":"text"},{"code":"children(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, vertices at one depth at least 1 apart along each subtree’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contour, and every parent centred over its first and last child. Where two subtrees had to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be pushed apart, the smaller subtrees between them are spaced evenly (Walker’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"improvement), so a mirrored tree draws as the reflection of the drawing and isomorphic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subtrees are drawn identically up to translation. Coordinates are ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" arithmetic:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"separations and centring alone give multiples of a power of ½, which are exact, but the even","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spacing divides a shift by the number of gaps it is spread over, so values such as ±5\/6","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"occur and are rounded (and a mirrored tree’s drawing then matches the reflection only to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rounding).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reingold and Tilford, “Tidier drawings of trees”, IEEE Transactions on Software"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Engineering SE-7(2), 1981."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Walker, “A node-positioning algorithm for general trees”, Software: Practice and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Experience 20(7), 1990."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert, “Improving Walker’s algorithm to run in linear time”,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Graph Drawing (GD 2002), LNCS 2528, 2002."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n) time and memory, with no recursion."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing":{"abstract":[],"title":"GraphDrawing","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Trees":{"title":"Trees","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Trees/RootedTree":{"type":"topic","title":"RootedTree","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees\/rootedtree","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RootedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Trees10RootedTreeV","text":"RootedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree","role":"symbol","abstract":[]},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Trees/RootedTree/reingoldTilfordLayout()":{"title":"reingoldTilfordLayout()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reingoldTilfordLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The tidy drawing of the tree: Reingold and Tilford’s layered tree drawing as Walker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refined it, in Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert’s linear-time form.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree\/reingoldTilfordLayout()","role":"symbol","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/trees\/rootedtree\/reingoldtilfordlayout()"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Drawing":{"type":"topic","title":"Drawing","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/drawing","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Drawing","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A position in the plane for each vertex, in a fixed vertex order: what every layout in this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module returns, and what a caller passes as a starting drawing.","type":"text"}]}}}